  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">School Centered Disaster Risk Reduction and Resilience to Climate Change in Haiti</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to strengthen the resilience of children and their families in the South and Grand&#x2019;Anse departments of Haiti to disaster and climate shocks and stresses through an integrated, full-spectrum response for children. The project will reinforce the capacities of national/local authorities and the civil society to cope with these risks; equip vulnerable children and their families with additional income, skills and competences to secure their livelihoods in the face of these risks; ensure access to quality education in a safe, inclusive and protective learning environment where children learn basic literacy and numeracy, in addition to socio-emotional skills, environment and climate action, with child safeguarding, gender and protection anchored to all programming to ensure their wellbeing; and empower children to be advocates and role models of environment and climate action.</narrative>
  </description>
